          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"the-tag-is-the-boundary\">The tag is the boundary</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">An org's own terralith: one estate, everything in it, one all-or-nothing\npermission boundary. The team wants per-team ownership without the\nstate-split engagement. Under choudoufu, ownership is two tags on the\nresource, and a plan reads only its own estate. So the decomposition\nstops being a project and becomes a metadata edit, and every step of it\nis an API call the account can refuse and does record.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Below, the story in phases. Each button runs one phase for real; the\npicture follows the run's own event log.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
